# GUARD — documentation is never benchmark scratch.
#
# The patterns above (`*_analysis.md`, `fuzzy_multimap_*.md`) were written for generated
# benchmark output at the repo root, but as bare globs they also match real documentation
# anywhere in the tree. They were silently excluding committed-worthy docs from version
# control — `docs/generalized/phase2d_analysis.md` (328 lines) and
# `docs/time_series/benchmark_analysis.md` (173 lines), both cross-linked from their sibling
# READMEs — so a fresh clone had dangling links to files that had never been committed.
#
# Re-include everything under `docs/`: nothing there is regenerable scratch. (Generated
# artifacts that DO live under docs/ — perf dumps, Coq .vo/.glob, flamegraphs — are ignored
# by extension elsewhere in this file, so this negation cannot un-ignore them.)
!docs/**/*.md

